    {
      "id": 39218,
      "name": "Rabit",
      "username": "Rabit",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-26T14:07:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>It’s not infinite because of one specific rule: a Power can only be used once in a turn.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slightly_smiling_face.png?v=9\" title=\":slightly_smiling_face:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slightly_smiling_face:\"> &nbsp;(Per page 6 of <a href=\"http://sentinelsofthemultiverse.com/system/files/downloads/Sentinels%20of%20the%20Multiverse%20Enhanced%20Edition%20Rulebook.pdf\">the Enhanced Edition rulebook</a>: “Even if a hero may use multiple powers in a turn, each instance of a power may only be used once per turn.”)</p>\n<p>So, while the Lyra will allow you to use another instrument (or even his base power), which might also allow you to use Inspiring Supertonic again, it won't let you use it's power again that turn; you'll eventually run out of powers you haven't already used in that turn.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:12:57.267Z",
