      "created_at": "2012-09-26T15:45:50.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Greonhal\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/bb73d2/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Greonhal:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Related question: Can Performs and Accompanies be used only once per turn, as well? That's how we've been playing it, but I can't recall seeing anything specific in the rules about that.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>No, they can be used multiple times in a turn.&nbsp; This is covered in the Infernal Relics rulebook describing Argent Adept.</p>",
